<br>

I don't know if an apology is in order. I don't know if an apology is right. I don't know if an apology is needed. I don't know if an apology can make it better.

<br>
<br>

What I do know is that I'm hurting, still. There hasn't been a day since where I haven't thought about the hole that's in my life now. Thinking that I'm missing a part of me that I needed to go on, that was essential, near the core of who I am. I do not think I can put into words the pain of absence I feel. 

<br>
<br>

The truth is that I miss you all. I am homesick for a time that doesn't exist anymore, that has passed, has moved on, has left me behind in a state of longing, unable to come to terms with the fact that it's gone. And I don't know what to do, don't know how to cope, worrying that the grief will never cease. Knowning that I've dismembered the floorboards beneath me, removed part of my foundation and leaving me struggling to keep my footing. All while knowing that It's my fault, that I hurt those I love by flailing about, not mature enough to just unclench my teeth to say out loud what needs to be said: that I'm a fool, ashamed of my own feelings, my own inadequacy the reason I keep hurting the people I mean to protect. That I'm not honest with myself, that I keep limiting myself, confining myself to a mental prison of my own making in order to try to appease everyone. Clutching so hard it hurts me and everyone else.

<br>
<br>

And all I can think of while typing this is that I'm melodramatic, that my feelings are wrong, to be pushed aside, I'm ashamed for these words. 